{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"subgraph_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"code":"AsSubgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SubDigraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"code":"filtered_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"metadata":{"title":"SubgraphView","externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubgraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L29"}},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with vertex holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"traps at construction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","title":"DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/EdgeRow":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeRow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/edgerow","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeRow"}],"title":"SubgraphView.EdgeRow","abstract":[{"text":"A row of positions (out-, in- or incident edges): the base’s, with the dropped edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped. The index row is stepped in step only when the view drops vertices.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedGraph-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"title":"DirectedGraph Implementations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directedgraph-implementations"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/UndirectedEdges":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges","title":"SubgraphView.UndirectedEdges","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/undirectededges","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The edges of an undirected ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubgraphView"},{"text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its positions.","type":"text"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Base","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","title":"SubgraphView","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"densely. Made by ","type":"text"},{"code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"subgraph_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"code":"AsSubgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SubDigraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"code":"filtered_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedEdges":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","title":"SubgraphView.DirectedEdges","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directededges","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The edges of a directed ","type":"text"},{"code":"SubgraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions. Stepping from one to the next skips the dropped ones.","type":"text"}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Base","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdges","kind":"identif